Title: The BASTA Protocol: Club Benefits, Compliance, and an Economic Design for Coordinated Military-Spending Reduction
Abstract: This paper proposes the BASTA Protocol, a mechanism design framework for coordinated reductions in military spending among states. The model integrates club benefits, compliance incentives, and economic design principles to address free-riding and enforcement challenges in arms control agreements. The protocol outlines a structured approach to cooperative security, emphasizing verifiable commitments and incentive-compatible mechanisms.
Keywords: defense economics; arms control; military spending; compliance design; economic incentives; international security
